o null and the module's `Required` answers 400. A to-one navigation is required unless declared `optional` (L-15a): `Relationship.IsRequiredToOne()` is read by `CreateSlots` (`SlotKindFor`), DMEFF011, DMEFF001 (a `create in` into a required to-one), DMREL006, the structural `IsRoot` and the host's `Unlink` (through `RelationshipContract.IsRequired`), while storage root-ness is the aggregate's (`OwnershipAggregatePass`: an entity nothing owns is a root), so the HTTP host's POST body carries each Required link as the target's route key (looked up like an action's entity argument, 404 when absent, preloaded from `ReadsOfCreate`, the action read walk entered at `Create`; `CreatesDirectly` refuses a target with a shadow key, and the seed skips every entity with a Required link), and `StorageAnalyzer` reads the published fact into `StorageNavigation.IsRequired` and `OnDelete` (an owned part cascades, any other required link restricts, an optional link stays ClientSetNull), which the DbContext generator declares per relationship (L-15b). The create-nav helper (`Create{Nav}`) and the entity's own `EnsureUnique` guard are not callees and pass through with no prefix, which keeps a unique assign's path the same whether or not the storage library rewrites it. `Guard` is set only for `Policy` (the real policy name, never `not_P`) and `Stage` (the stage name). The receiver prints fully qualified (`Poly.Runtime.DomainFailure`), so a member, enum, value type or entity named `Poly` shadows it: `Poly` and `System` are reserved for every entity and as an action parameter name for every action, and `DomainResult` is reserved as an action parameter name for an action with no result members (void actions call `DomainResult.Success()` / `.Failure(…)` in expression position; a merged void/typed stage-dispatched copy is deliberately over-rejected). `ReservedNames.TryReservedAsActionParameter` reads each row's `AppliesToAction` predicate. `ModuleOutcome` carries the lowered body's `Poly.Runt